    {
      "id": "l-t",
      "name": "Title Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -336
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# GHL Adapter (Live)\n\nThe real GoHighLevel adapter. Same input and output contract as the mock adapter. Talks to GoHighLevel with the native HighLevel nodes (contact, opportunity) and, where the node has no operation (tags, opportunity search, notes), with HTTP requests that use the same 'HighLevel account' OAuth2 credential.\n\n**Called by:** the four handler workflows (chosen by 'ghl_adapter_id' in the main workflow's Store Settings). **Standalone-capable:** no.\n\n**Sections:** 1. Route the call. 2. Upsert contact, tags and stage. 3. Record the SMS as a contact note.\n\n**Before use:** set the GoHighLevel location, pipeline and stage IDs in 'adapter_config' in the main workflow's Store Settings. On a new n8n server, reconnect the 'HighLevel account' credential (GoHighLevel refresh tokens are single-use).",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 1700,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l-1",
      "name": "Section 1 Note - Route The Call",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Route the call\n\nTriggered by: a handler workflow calling this one (Execute Workflow).\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Receives the adapter input (action, email, phone, names, target stage, tags, SMS text, adapter_config).\n2. Reads the GoHighLevel IDs from adapter_config.\n3. Routes to 'upsert_stage' or 'send_sms' by the action.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l-2",
      "name": "Section 2 Note - Upsert Contact Tags And Stage",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        688,
        32
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Upsert contact, tags and stage\n\nTriggered by: runs inline after 'Route the call' when action = upsert_stage.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Creates or updates the contact by email (GoHighLevel upsert).\n2. Adds tags, removes tags (only when there are any).\n3. Looks for the contact's opportunity in the pipeline.\n4. Decides: create it, move it forward, or leave it (never moves backwards).\n5. Returns ok, contact_id, opportunity_id, stage_before, stage_applied, tags_final.",
        "height": 780,
        "width": 2560,
        "color": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "l-3",
      "name": "Section 3 Note - Send SMS",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        688,
        864
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Record the SMS as a contact note\n\nTriggered by: runs inline after 'Route the call' when action = send_sms.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Finds (or creates) the contact by email.\n2. Adds the SMS text to the contact as a note 'SMS (demo, not sent): ...'. The demo sandbox has no phone number and SMS costs money; for a real send, replace this node with a POST to /conversations/messages (type SMS) using the same credential.\n3. Returns ok, sms_sent (true when the note was saved), error. A failure does not stop the caller (soft fail).",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 1200,
        "color": 5
      }
    },
